. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 *
. *
. * Estimate whether having at least one daughter predicts more progressive
. * gender attitudes, using data from private household respondents with childr
> en 
. * in 2019.
. *
. * Model specification:
. *   - Outcome: gender_attitudes (summed index of six items, cleaned of negati
> ves)
. *   - Key predictor: having_daughter (1 if any daughter born before interview
>  year)
. *   - Prespecified covariates:
. *       • sumkids            = total number of biological children
. *       • hghinc             = monthly household net income (EUR)
. *       • female             = respondent’s sex (2 =female, 1 =male)
. *       • age_at_int       = age at time of interview (2019)
. *       • erwerb             = employment status (1–4 categories)
. *       • pld0131_v2         = marital status (coded; invalid → missing)
. *       • plh0258_v9         = religious affiliation (coded; invalid → missin
> g)
. *       • migback            = migration background indicator
. *       • sampreg            = geographic region of sample (east/west)
. *       • pgpsbil            = school-leaving degree
. *
. * We supplement these controls with a LASSO-based, data-driven selection
. * implemented via dsregress. The selected variables (from `numvars`) are
. * stored in e(controls_sel) — duplicates are automatically dropped by Stata.
. * 
. * The LASSO can pick from the following list of variables:
. *               • corigin                     = Country of origin (country of
>  birth) of the respondent (ISO numeric country codes)
. *               • fprofedu                    = Father’s highest completed pr
> ofessional education
. *               • mprofedu                    = Mother’s highest completed pr
> ofessional education
. *               • locchildh           = Place where respondent was raised to 
> age 15; 1=Large city, 2=Medium city, 3=Small city, 4=Countryside
. *               • hlf0135                     = Residential area—distance of 
> dwelling to city centre; 1=City‑centre flat, 2=<10 km, 3=10–<25 km, 4=25–<40 
> km, 5=40–<60 km, 6=≥60 km
. *               • hlf0151                     = Respondent’s level of worry a
> bout crime in their neighbourhood; 1=Not worried … 4=Very worried
. *               • nums                                = Number of sisters rep
> orted by respondent
. *               • numb                                = Number of brothers re
> ported by respondent
. *
. * Inference approach:
. *   • Step 1: LASSO to identify additional relevant covariates
. *   • Step 2: OLS regression including both prespecified and LASSO selected
. *             controls, with robust standard errors to mitigate collinearity
. *             and heteroskedasticity concerns.
. *
. * Step 1: LASSO-based selection of controls
. version 16.0: dsregress gender_attitudes having_daughter, ///
>     controls((sumkids hghinc i.female age_at_int i.erwerb ///
>              i.pld0131_v2 ib(6).plh0258_v9 i.migback sampreg ///
>              i.pgpsbil) `numvars') rseed(10101)
6b.plh0258_v9 omitted

